{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00148",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.31,
      "end_seconds": 5.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. Can I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.21,
      "end_seconds": 9.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What's the problem?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 10.91,
      "end_seconds": 15.92,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.91,
      "end_seconds": 21.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Alright, good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.55,
      "end_seconds": 30.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.68,
      "text": "Um, so... a red eye. That's why I came. I didn't want to make a fuss, you know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.05,
      "end_seconds": 34.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 36.03,
      "end_seconds": 42.68,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.16,
      "end_seconds": 49.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.44,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.6,
      "end_seconds": 53.03,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "I'd say moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.12,
      "end_seconds": 57.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "And what do you do to cope with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.33,
      "end_seconds": 63.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "I get some relief from a cold compress."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 65.05,
      "end_seconds": 67.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.66,
      "end_seconds": 71.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "It usually comes with itching."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.51,
      "end_seconds": 78.79,
      "duration_seconds": 7.28,
      "text": "And, And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 78.89,
      "end_seconds": 84.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.77,
      "end_seconds": 91.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.31,
      "text": "I was getting to that! The itching? That's been since Friday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.27,
      "end_seconds": 96.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "On a normal day, how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.99,
      "end_seconds": 104.28,
      "duration_seconds": 6.29,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.97,
      "end_seconds": 110.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.46,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.15,
      "end_seconds": 113.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.01,
      "end_seconds": 121.32,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "Okay, have you had a red eye before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.61,
      "end_seconds": 127.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "A bit, last year. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 129.24,
      "end_seconds": 131.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Mm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 136.14,
      "end_seconds": 144.43,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Saturation 97 percent, heart rate 73, temperature 36.7. BP is 121 over 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.46,
      "end_seconds": 146.45,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.6,
      "end_seconds": 151.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Let me examine, it won't take long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.92,
      "end_seconds": 156.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Stay still while I have a look."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.14,
      "end_seconds": 181.33,
      "duration_seconds": 8.19,
      "text": "The white of the eye is pink all over, and there's some sticky discharge on the lashes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.39,
      "end_seconds": 184.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Let me look at this properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.58,
      "end_seconds": 202.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Your vision is normal on the chart and the pupil reacts well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.01,
      "end_seconds": 205.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "Mm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.55,
      "end_seconds": 218.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.97,
      "text": "Right, you can sit back down. Did you get pain in the eye or contact lens?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.98,
      "end_seconds": 233.42,
      "duration_seconds": 13.44,
      "text": "No, no pain in the eye, no contact lens. I did have a sticky discharge in the morning at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.38,
      "end_seconds": 241.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "Have you had any foreign body in the eye, loss of vision, sensitivity to light or cold?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.31,
      "end_seconds": 256.16,
      "duration_seconds": 8.85,
      "text": "No, no foreign body in the eye, loss of vision, sensitivity to light or cold."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.66,
      "end_seconds": 261.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.68,
      "end_seconds": 265.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Okay, so no weakness or anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.04,
      "end_seconds": 268.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.5,
      "end_seconds": 271.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "No problems with breathing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 273.36,
      "end_seconds": 275.33,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 277.42,
      "end_seconds": 282.42,
      "duration_seconds": 5.0,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.0,
      "end_seconds": 285.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.3,
      "end_seconds": 290.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "I smoke about ten cigarettes a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.28,
      "end_seconds": 292.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "How about exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 296.34,
      "end_seconds": 299.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.51,
      "text": "Not really, I don't get much exercise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.9,
      "end_seconds": 304.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.98,
      "end_seconds": 310.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.66,
      "text": "It's hydrocortisone cream, when needed for the eczema."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 311.34,
      "end_seconds": 318.33,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "He is supposed to take it when needed, but I can't say he always does."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.78,
      "end_seconds": 335.91,
      "duration_seconds": 16.13,
      "text": "It's iron tablets, once a day. I take escitalopram, 10 milligrams, once a day for the anxiety. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.27,
      "end_seconds": 339.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "When did you start it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.07,
      "end_seconds": 345.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "About two months. Metformin, twice a day for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.53,
      "end_seconds": 349.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.6,
      "end_seconds": 352.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "It's 500 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.41,
      "end_seconds": 356.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.58,
      "end_seconds": 363.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.41,
      "text": "For two months. I had glimepiride at one point, but I'm off it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.98,
      "end_seconds": 377.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 378.61,
      "end_seconds": 385.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "I've had eczema, yes. I've got low haemoglobin. I've had anxiety, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 386.93,
      "end_seconds": 387.63,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 389.37,
      "end_seconds": 391.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "I've got diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.92,
      "end_seconds": 401.96,
      "duration_seconds": 10.04,
      "text": "Okay, I can see anxiety and diabetes in your file as well. So, have you had to have anything operated on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 407.29,
      "end_seconds": 411.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "I had my appendix out about eight years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 412.88,
      "end_seconds": 416.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.93,
      "end_seconds": 423.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.24,
      "end_seconds": 429.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "Any relatives with health problems I should be aware of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 429.93,
      "end_seconds": 432.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "My grandmother had breast cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 434.0,
      "end_seconds": 444.93,
      "duration_seconds": 10.93,
      "text": "From what you've told me and what I found, I don't have a clear answer today: conjunctivitis is possible, and so is an allergic eye problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 446.64,
      "end_seconds": 450.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Is this something I'll have for good?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 451.0,
      "end_seconds": 457.78,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like conjunctivitis, but I'd like to confirm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 466.05,
      "end_seconds": 489.61,
      "duration_seconds": 23.56,
      "text": "Let's book an eye swab to look into red eye. I'm going to put you on chloramphenicol eye drops, four times a day, for five days. That's for conjunctivitis. Wash your hands often, don't share towels, and don't rub the eye. We'll catch up if it's not better in three days. Good. Let us know how you get on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 493.84,
      "end_seconds": 499.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "I think that's clear. Thank you for being so thorough."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 500.72,
      "end_seconds": 501.42,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Goodbye."
    }
  ]
}